  // Issue #3387: the file set `tsc --noEmit` verifies for this package.
  //
  // tsconfig.json is what typescript-eslint resolves source files against, so
  // it must not exclude a file that lives in this package. An excluded file
  // belongs to no package project and falls back to the root tsconfig.json,
  // which declares no `include` and therefore spans the whole repository.
  // Building that program cost ~7 GB and ~40 s per ESLint process, and one
  // such file was enough to pay it in full.
  //
  // tsconfig.json therefore keeps only node_modules, dist, and entries that
  // point outside this package; this file carries the complete list and is
  // what `tsc` reads. The overlap is deliberate, because `extends` replaces
  // `exclude` wholesale rather than merging it.
  // scripts/tests/tsconfig-project-coverage.test.ts holds both halves to that.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  // Set here as well as on the command line so a direct
  // `tsc -p tsconfig.noemit.json` cannot emit build output into the sources.
  "compilerOptions": { "noEmit": true },
